  "limits": [
    "All 21 retained command line images, 21 SDK line images and 14 plane images pass exact 1e-6 control-distance admission under explicitly matched normalized charts. Endpoint orientation, physical knot domains and surface normal signs remain raw comparison data; no directed parity claim is made.",
    "The kernel preserves exact collinear lines and uses the shared exactly centered thin SVD for other point sets. Repeated largest singular values admit multiple optimal lines. The retained square matches its native image, but general ambiguous configurations remain unqualified.",
    "Each repeated point and each full mesh/cloud vertex contributes equally; selected grips use Euclidean locations. Exact scalar products bound all input projections. The stored endpoint distance must remain finite and nonzero. Coordinate normalization can reject unresolved numerical ranges rather than silently collapsing input.",
    "The original one-million-point plane fit cap remains, with an equal line-fit cap. Existing plane error policy and all model/certificate tolerances remain. Line fits admit short representable geometry through the existing validated line representation instead of a model-distance collapse gate.",
    "A coincident line selection accepts a no-output command, retaining Redo and clearing only postselected object picks. The plane no-result policy still declines. Whole mesh selection is eligible for lines; the plane command still requires point/cloud objects or selected grips. Native source/metadata and local Undo/Redo/cancellation/viewport tests remain separate evidence.",
    "All runtime tests and the local protocol export use the default debug build. Workspace clippy checks all targets with native-smlib enabled. No new native C++ code, sanitizer run or performance qualification is claimed. Upstream N_LineFit3dPts forms a covariance-derived normal matrix; this path reuses the existing centered thin SVD instead of introducing a second solver."
  ],
